    "slip_type": "variable",
    "smoothing_constraint": true,
    "notes": "Figure 5 slip color contours manually/reproducibly approximated by color-scale matching on a regular 2-km display grid. Samples are not the original inversion mesh or published individual patch amplitudes; values outside colored region are assigned zero, while inside-region sample estimates have figure-resolution uncertainty. Center of plotted coordinates is the hypocenter (star). Image y positive is upward (shallower), with absolute depth approx 24-y km. The paper reports main peak ~1.25 m ~4 km WNW of hypocenter, secondary smaller concentration ~32 km depth to ESE, mean slip ~0.19 m over ruptured area. The abstract gives event latitude 36.441 longitude 28.904 while Table 1 reports 36.468 28.888, both at 24 km depth; abstract coordinates used here. Chosen rake 171 degrees from Table 1, not a patch-specific rake inversion. The stated fault grid covers the illustrated +/-14 km plot bounds rather than the actual published mesh. Publication DOI independently verified on journal website."
  },
